          deckDescription: 'Dong Guan Pai (Dongguan cards): a 120-card pack used in Guangdong. It has three numeral suits (ben, suo, wan) with ranks 1 to 9, plus three odd cards (da hong, xiao hong, ba shu) that count as ones. There are four identical copies of each of the 30 unique cards, making 120 cards total. The pack is used for pair-collection and draw-and-discard play.',
          suitDescription: 'Three money-suited suits: ben (coins), suo (strings), and wan (myriads), each with ranks 1 through 9. The three odd cards (da hong, xiao hong, ba shu) have no suit but count as rank one for pairing. Cards are typically narrow and long, held in a fan shape.',
          rankDescription: 'Numerals 1 to 9 in each of the three suits; the three odd cards (da hong, xiao hong, ba shu) count as ones and can pair with each other or with suit ones to form a Ka (same number, different suits). Dui are identical cards; Ka are same number, different suits.',
          dealPattern: 'Dealer receives six cards first; then cards are dealt in fives anticlockwise for three rounds. Dealer ends with 16 cards, each other player with 15. Remainder forms the stock.',
